 of modal interpretations. It is shown that despite its classicality, the proposed logic is empirically indistinguishable from quantum logic.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1086/289967", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2008, 1, 4]], "date-time": "2008-01-04T13:54:51Z", "timestamp": 1199454891000}, "page": "S322-S329", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["Logical Foundations for Modal Interpretations of Quantum Mechanics"], "prefix": "10.1017", "volume": "63", "author": [{"given": "Michael", "family": "Dickson", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "56", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2022, 4, 1]]}, "reference": [{"key": "S0031824800075450_R12", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1093/0198239807.001.0001"}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R10", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF02304905"}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R3", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00670775"}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R6", "unstructured": "Dickson, M. (1996), ‘On the Plurality of Dynamics: Transition Probabilities and Modal Interpretations’, forthcoming in R. Healey and G. Hellman (eds.), Minnesota Studies in the Philosophy of Science."}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S1355-2198(96)00002-0"}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R11", "volume-title": "Philosophic Foundations of Quantum Mechanics", "author": "Reichenbach", "year": "1944"}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R7", "first-page": "481", "article-title": "‘Les Relations d'Incertitude de Heisenberg et la Logique’", "volume": "204", "author": "Fevrier", "year": "1937", "journal-title": "Comptes Rendus Hebdomadaires des Séances de l'Académie des Sciences"}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R5", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF02186577"}, {"key": "S0031824800075450_R8", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1111/j.1746-8361.1978.tb01319.x"